# REQ-014: Confidentiality & Visibility Settings

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Medium
**Risk:** High (confidentiality breaches are patient safety and IG incidents)
**Depends On:** REQ-012 (Filing), REQ-009 (Audit Trail), REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox)

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator or clinician,
I need to control whether a document is confidential and whether it is visible to the patient online,
So that sensitive documents are protected in line with practice confidentiality policies and patient preferences.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] **The Confidentiality and Patient Online Visibility controls are accessible inline from the document filing panel** during the standard filing workflow. Users do not need to navigate to a separate settings screen to set these values at the time of filing. *(Must Have — cross-ref REQ-001)*
- [ ] A document can be marked as confidential at the time of filing. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Confidentiality access control honours the existing EMIS Web confidentiality policies — the same rules that govern document visibility in EMIS Web apply in EMIS-X Documents Manager. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] A user with appropriate authority can override the confidentiality policy for a specific document. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] All confidentiality overrides are audited — who overrode, which document, when, and what the previous and new confidentiality state was. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Patient online visibility can be controlled per document — a document can be marked as visible or not visible to the patient via online record access (e.g. NHS App / Patient Access). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Patient online visibility defaults to **not visible to patient** unless explicitly set otherwise. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Confidentiality defaults to **Standard access** unless explicitly changed. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] When either default (Standard access or Not visible to patient) is changed during filing, a visible warning is displayed to the user confirming the non-default choice. *(Must Have — CLIN-007, CLIN-010)*
- [ ] Changes to patient online visibility are audited. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Confidentiality status and patient online visibility are displayed clearly on the document in the care record so users can see the current state without opening a settings panel. *(Must Have)*

