## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — all confidentiality changes and overrides audited before taking effect
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — confidentiality status and patient visibility state must be clearly visible on the document at all times
- **CLIN-009:** Clinical Safety Logging — confidentiality override events logged as safety-critical events using ERN identifiers
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — confidentiality policy enforcement must fail closed; if policy cannot be evaluated, default to most restrictive access

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-042:** Confidential document visible to unauthorised user — sensitive clinical information (e.g. sexual health, mental health) accessed without appropriate authority
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Critical

- **HAZ-DOC-043:** Confidential document visible to patient online without authorisation — patient sees sensitive information before appropriate clinical review
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low–Medium (if patient visibility defaults to visible)
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-044:** Confidentiality override not audited — access control change undetectable; potential data breach not evidenced
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-045:** Confidentiality policy not honoured due to EMIS Web/X policy sync failure — document treated as non-confidential when it should be restricted
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-041:** Confidentiality and patient visibility state displayed on document; not hidden in settings panel
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-042:** Patient online visibility defaults to not visible; opt-in required
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-043:** All confidentiality and visibility changes audited before taking effect; override captures before/after state
  - **Type:** Observability
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-044:** Confidentiality policy evaluation fails closed — if EMIS Web policy cannot be retrieved, most restrictive access applied
  - **Type:** Error Handling
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

