## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-002:** Privacy by Design and Default — patient online visibility defaults to not visible; confidentiality defaults to most restrictive applicable policy
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data; confidentiality obligations under common law duty of confidence
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — confidential documents are special category data; encrypted at rest; access strictly controlled
- **IG-005:** Data Subject Rights — patient online visibility directly affects patient's ability to exercise Article 15 (right of access); changes must be auditable and defensible
- **IG-008:** Consent Management — patient online visibility changes are a consent-adjacent action; must be auditable
- **IG-009:** Data Breach Notification — unauthorised access to a confidential document is a data breach; must be detectable via audit

### Data Handling
- Confidentiality status stored as a structured flag on the document record; not embedded in the document file
- Patient online visibility flag stored per document; separate from confidentiality flag
- Confidentiality policy resolution references EMIS Web policy definitions; EMIS-X does not maintain a separate policy store
- Override audit entries capture: user ERN, document ERN, previous state, new state, timestamp, reason (if captured)

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 5(1)(f):** Integrity and confidentiality — confidential documents protected from unauthorised access
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category health data — medical purposes; enhanced protection required
- **Article 15:** Right of access — patient online visibility setting affects what patients can access

