### Component Specifications

> 🚫 All interactive elements use `@emisgroup/ui-*` exclusively.

**Confidentiality Select (in Filing form):**
- `Select aria-label={t('filing.confidentiality.label')}`
- Options (from EMIS Web policy): Standard access / Restricted — clinical staff only / Confidential — GP & admin lead only
- Default: Standard access
- On change from default: `Banner variant="warning"` inline: `{t('filing.confidentiality.changedWarning')}`
- Selected Restricted: field tinted `var(--cautionary)` tint; bold label
- Selected Confidential: field tinted `var(--negative)` tint; bold label

**Patient Online Visibility Select:**
- `Select aria-label={t('filing.onlineVisibility.label')}`
- Options: Not visible to patient (default — IG-002) / Visible to patient
- Default: Not visible to patient — MANDATORY (HAZ-DOC-043)
- On change from default: same `Banner variant="warning"` pattern

**Fail-Closed Defaults Notice (always shown when either control is present):**
- `Banner variant="warning"` — persistent during filing step; cannot be dismissed
- Copy confirms both defaults and that change should only be made if clinically appropriate

**Confidentiality Status Badge (document list row + viewer header):**
- Standard: `Badge variant="inactive"` `{t('confidentiality.standard')}` + `~icons/ic/outline-lock-open` 16px
- Restricted: `Badge variant="info"` `{t('confidentiality.restricted')}` + `~icons/ic/outline-lock` 16px + `var(--cautionary)` tint
- Confidential: `Badge variant="primary"` `{t('confidentiality.confidential')}` + `~icons/ic/outline-lock` 16px + `var(--negative)` tint

**Override Flow (Post-Filing):**
- "Change confidentiality": `Button variant="mono" size="small"` visible only to authorised roles (server-side role check; also hidden client-side)
